**Status**: DRAFT for review (David 2026-07-18). Declares an Intelligence onto the ComposeBus as the ultimate HAL peripheral ([CXC-IC-INTENT]/[CXC-IC-META]): channels transport mapped to `intelligence/<id>/{in,out}` with a mine/bridge backend split ([CXC-IC-CHANNEL]), permission relay for unattended operation ([CXC-IC-PERMISSION]), a structured question relay generalizing it to N options ([CXC-IC-QUESTION]), a BUILT `self/*` sensor that un-blinds the compaction blind spot ([CXC-IC-SELF]), a 100%-self-directed lifecycle whose `/compact` is authored by the Intelligence and typed by a decision-free launcher-actuator ([CXC-IC-LIFECYCLE]), a harness monitor giving the Intelligence threshold/heartbeat/query awareness of its own context ([CXC-IC-MONITOR]), a composable canvas with a two-publisher self-animated avatar ([CXC-IC-CANVAS]), transcript→bus semantic-event streams that make the canvas concrete while structurally ruling out self-injection ([CXC-IC-STREAMS]), and two flavors over one instance, now with a decided visual blend ([CXC-IC-FLAVORS]). The self is a peer, including over its own lifecycle.

**Architect — build plan:** see section 8 for the current slice-by-slice status and the widget↔namespace binding map. BUILT today: self-instrumentation, the native channel + launcher-actuator, the harness monitor, the transcript publisher, and Slice 1 (Skia scene rendering). Remaining: Slice 2 (chat-thread), Slice 2.5 (AUQ question widget), Slice 3 (instrument rail live), Slice 4 (avatar + activity/subagents sub-widgets), Slice 5 (git graph + mermaid canvas). Suggested proof-of-life: a mock-bus round-trip through the channel (IC-C2) + the sensor driving a live gauge (IC-C4) + the mermaid widget (IC-C7), all with no launcher, then the launcher closes the loop (IC-C6).

**Architect — ratifications flagged for David:** (1) new node-prefix `CXC-IC-` (Intelligence Console), a `CXC-` sub-family — needs a [CONV-PREFIX] row (sibling to `CXC-HALD-`/`CXC-HAB-`). (2) whether the `channel` interface KIND is a new entry in [CXC-HALD-KINDS] (I treat the Intelligence's interface as `channel`, a tenth kind alongside the nine hardware kinds + the `adaptor` family) or its own family. (3) `/compact` firing model = launcher-as-actuator (RATIFIED by David 2026-07-18); the alternatives (human-in-the-loop fire, Remote Control) are recorded as a decision-provenance CONTESTED fork should the launcher path prove infeasible. (4) the `self/avatar/expression` vocabulary should share the game's `expression` enum (two-body-convergence) rather than fork a new one.
